            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Harnessing the Human Side of Transformations"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 1
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                476,
                772,
                626
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "By Tuukka Seppä, Kristy Ellmer, Julia Dhar, Simon Weinstein, Garett Chau, Paul Catchlove, and Connor Currier"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                656,
                784,
                695
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "ARTICLE APRIL 27, 2026 8 MIN READ"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                719,
                363,
                736
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The imperative for companies to transform is growing, but organizational transformations have a low success rate. According to BCG research, only about one in four succeeds in capturing short-term and long-term value. What sets the best, most successful transformations apart? A growing body of research from BCG's Bruce Henderson Institute and the firm's Behavioral Science Lab points to a crucial factor: a human-centric approach."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                796,
                942,
                898
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footer",
            "content": {
                "page_footer_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "©2026 Boston Consulting Group"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                43,
                969,
                249,
                984
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "content": {
                "page_number_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "1"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                942,
                970,
                954,
                983
            ]
        }
    ],
    [
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Human-centric transformations are grounded in, and informed by, principles of behavioral science—an understanding of how people act in different contexts—to predict behavior and design techniques and practices that can help achieve target outcomes. This type of transformation isn’t always easy. It requires elevating people at all levels, from top executives to frontline employees, to the center of the change process and tapping into their collective effort. But the approach can be learned, and it leads to measurably better transformation outcomes."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                67,
                942,
                186
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Companies that undertake human-centric transformations see faster scaling of initiatives, increased human capacity and capital within the organization, and better financial outcomes. In our experience supporting hundreds of transformations across industries, companies that make holistic, people-centered change management an integral part of the transformation outperform their peers by 15% in total shareholder return."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                200,
                944,
                300
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "The Power of Human-Centric Change"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 1
            },
            "bbox": [
                42,
                369,
                772,
                450
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "All transformations require considering the why, what, and how of the overall program. (See the exhibit.) True success hinges on a human-centric approach across all three:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                476,
                922,
                516
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "• Why: Articulating the overarching purpose for undertaking the transformation now"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                545,
                831,
                565
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- What: Identifying the financial and operational objectives that must be met to create greater value—revenue growth, cost reduction, a stronger balance sheet, or some combination of the three—all aligned with the company strategy"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                580,
                932,
                640
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- How: Developing the behaviors, mindsets, organizational structure, tools, capabilities, and processes to make change happen and ensure that it sticks"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                655,
                905,
                695
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footer",
            "content": {
                "page_footer_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "©2026 Boston Consulting Group"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                43,
                970,
                249,
                984
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "content": {
                "page_number_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "2"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                942,
                970,
                954,
                983
            ]
        }
    ],
    [
        {
            "type": "title",
            "content": {
                "title_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Transformations Are More Likely to Succeed When They Address Three Elements"
                    }
                ],
                "level": 1
            },
            "bbox": [
                43,
                63,
                681,
                103
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "chart",
            "content": {
                "image_source": {
                    "path": "images/01d8d9197a0b085dd3635ee60d178387b3b19d1400b81435f73f7be60c1d18a7.jpg"
                },
                "content": "",
                "chart_caption": [],
                "chart_footnote": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Source: BCG."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                43,
                116,
                725,
                381
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "Here we focus on the “how” element, which is where a human-centric approach is crucial. Transformations rely on people’s willingness to change and do things differently, yet people are naturally averse to change. By applying best practices from behavioral science to address this aversion, transformations can achieve better and more lasting outcomes."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                513,
                934,
                594
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "We have strong evidence of the power of human-centric change. Specifically, we see the following increases in the likelihood of sustained performance improvements through a people-based approach to transformation:"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                607,
                944,
                667
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- 90% when holistic, people-centered change management is an integral part of the transformation"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                696,
                829,
                734
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- 27% when leaders are aligned on their roles and responsibilities in the transformation and can shape the behaviors of people on their team."
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                751,
                909,
                791
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- 21% when a chief transformation officer is in place with sufficient authority to lead the transformation, challenge the status quo, and lead the overall workforce"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                804,
                865,
                846
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": {
                "paragraph_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "- 19% when all people in the organization are clear about what needs to change, how they can contribute, and how their work will evolve"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                40,
                860,
                925,
                898
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_footer",
            "content": {
                "page_footer_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "©2026 Boston Consulting Group"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                43,
                969,
                249,
                984
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "page_number",
            "content": {
                "page_number_content": [
                    {
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "3"
                    }
                ]
            },
            "bbox": [
                942,
                970,
